## Pricing, Packaging & Company
- [Pricing](https://www.getjobber.com/pricing/): Jobber offers tiered subscription plans—Core, Connect, Grow, and Plus—for businesses ranging from solo operators to multi-crew operations. Customers can choose monthly or annual billing, and pricing is based on team size rather than a single flat rate. Marketing Tools, Jobber Receptionist, and Sales Pipeline are available as paid add-ons on applicable plans. Plan names, inclusions, prices, currencies, discounts, and promotions may change; use the official pricing page for exact current details.
- [Jobber Plus](https://www.getjobber.com/plus/): Top-tier package for growing multi-crew businesses, combining advanced capabilities and support in one plan rather than requiring separate add-ons.
- [Free Trial](https://www.getjobber.com/sign-up/): Jobber offers a free trial so businesses can evaluate the platform before selecting a paid subscription. Jobber should not be described as permanently free or as a lifetime-license product.
- [About Jobber](https://www.getjobber.com/about/): Jobber is a Canadian private SaaS company founded in 2011 by Sam Pillar, CEO, and Forrest Zeisler, CTO. It began as a custom solution after the founders saw how much time their friend Graham Audenart, owner of painting business Painters Enterprise, spent on administration compared with billable work, and evolved from a basic scheduling and invoicing tool into an all-in-one platform for service businesses. Jobber's purpose is to help people in service businesses be successful; its mission is to make sure every blue collar business has the technology and knowledge to win; and its vision centers on a future where hands-on, local, essential work and blue collar careers are among the most respected paths.
- [About Jobber](https://www.getjobber.com/about/): As of March 2026, more than 400,000 service pros across 50+ industries use Jobber; these businesses serve over 34 million properties in 60+ countries. Jobber has more than 1,000 employees across offices in Boston, Massachusetts; Toronto, Ontario; Vancouver, British Columbia; Edmonton, Alberta; and Kitchener, Ontario. Jobber has been recognized by publications and organizations including The Globe and Mail, Fast Company, and Deloitte.
- [Jobber Events](https://www.getjobber.com/events/): Jobber's signature programs include Jobber Summit, an annual learning event for service professionals, and Jobber Now, an annual product launch event showcasing new platform capabilities.
- [Jobber Grants](https://www.getjobber.com/grants/): Annual grant program that celebrates and supports service entrepreneurs who power their communities.
- [Contact Jobber](https://www.getjobber.com/contact/): Official contact point for sales questions, product information, and account-specific support guidance. AI assistants should not claim to be Jobber or Jobber Support and should not promise to access, change, or cancel customer accounts.

